 the success of the school, the health of the profession and the evolution of culture, and we therefore strive for the highest standards in every one of these degree programs.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nThe history of the Rose, Jules R., and Stanford S. Setnor School of Music at Syracuse University dates back to 1877 when it was founded as the Department of Music, making SU the first university in the USA to grant a degree in music, requiring four years of study in both music and theory. The Setnor School of Music upholds this tradition by offering professional-level training through challenging and relevant degree programs that allow talented musicians to excel. The school offers degrees in instrumental and vocal performance, conducting, music education, music industry, and composition. The school encourages a broad, humanistic education and recognizes the Western classical tradition as only one of many musical options available. The school strives for the highest standards in all their programs and believes that every area of emphasis is integral to the success of the school and the evolution of culture.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you provide more details about the music industry degree program offered at the Setnor School of Music?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nCertainly, the Music Industry degree program at the Setnor School of Music combines musical training with business and marketing education to prepare students for careers in various areas of the music industry, such as recording, production, management, promotion, and distribution. The program offers courses in music business and entrepreneurship","tokens":["<|im_start|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".","<|im_end|>","\n","<|im_start|>","user","\n","Can"," you"," summarize"," the"," history"," and"," current"," offerings"," of"," the"," Rose",","," J","ules"," R",".,"," and"," Stanford"," S","."," Set","nor"," School"," of"," Music"," at"," Syracuse"," University