:"The weather today is","baseline":" sunny. It's a good day to go for a walk. I'm going to the park. I'm going to","ablated":" sunny. It's a good day to go for a walk. I'm going to the park. I'm going to","clamped":[" sunny. It is ________ than yesterday.____\nA. hot\nB. colder\nC. hotter\n答案"," sunny. It is ________ than yesterday.____\nA. hot\nB. colder\nC. hotter\n答案"," sunny. It is ________ than yesterday.____\nA. hot\nB. colder\nC. hotter\nD"]},{"prompt":"I went to the shop and bought","baseline":" a lot of things. I ________ a lot of things. A. bought B. bought C. am buying D","ablated":" a lot of things. I ________ a lot of things. A. bought B. bought C. am buying D","clamped":[" a lot of things. I ________ a lot of things. A. bought B. bought C. am buying D"," a lot of things．（改为同义句） I bought a lot of things____ the shop．\nat\n\n"," a new pair of shoes．（同义句转换） I bought a new pair of shoes____．\n\nin the"]},{"prompt":"The best way to learn is","baseline":" to do it. This is the motto of the University of the Philippines (UP) and the University of the Philippines Health","ablated":" to do it. This is the motto of the University of the Philippines (UP) and the University of the Philippines Health","clamped":[" to do it. This is the motto of the University of the West of England (UWE) and the University of"," to do it. This is the motto of the University of the West of England (UWE) and the University of"," to use it. This is the motto of the National Institute of Education (NIE), a private educational institute in the"]},{"prompt":"Once upon a time,","baseline":" there was a little girl named Lily. She loved to play with her toys and watch the stars. One day, she","ablated":" there was a little girl named Lily. She loved to play with her toys and watch the stars. One day, she","clamped":[" there was a little girl named Lily. She loved to play with her toys and watch the stars. One day, she"," there was a little girl named Lily. She loved to play with her toys and explore the world around her. One day"," there was a little girl named Lily. She loved to play with her toys. One day, she found a strange toy"]},{"prompt":"The report concluded that","baseline":" the 2010 census showed that the population of the United States was 318,000","ablated":" the 2010 census showed that the population of the United States was 328,000","clamped":[" the 2010 census showed that the population of the United States was 318,000"," the 2010 census showed that the population of the country was 110 million, up from "," the country's economic growth rate was 5.5 percent in 2015, which was the highest in"]}]},"wordnet_specificity":null,"supersedes":null,"sister_of":null,"opposite_pole":{"pole":"positive","top_examples":[{"text":"Q:\n\nGridView WebForm having multiple checkboxes per row but only 1 per row is allowed to be checked\n\nI have code in which a gridview in asp.net webforms spits out 3 checkboxes of which I would like to have Jquery easily traverse through the ID's and ONLY allow 1 checkbox per row to be checked.  \nThey will Always have the same name just that the ending numbers will increase  thus row 1 might not have a number,  but then ending in 1  then ending in 2  , then they all end of 3  etc...\nI could do this regretfully long way of writing a ton of javascript/jquery in which I check for each specific checkbox and those that end in 1, those cannot have any others ending with 1 to be checked, they have to be unchecked.\nI was thinking about regex in which I check the beginning of the ID and then the end of the ID and making sense that per ID having \"chkCtrl\" AND ending with a unique number like \"1\"  that the specific box being checked will uncheck the other \"chkCtrl\" ending in 1  .  Thus  Out1 , Y1 , N1   \nI'm sure that there IS a fast way to do this I just cannot seem to find an example of it.  \nExample \n<table>\n<tr>\n    <td>Out</td>\n    <td>Yes</td>\n    <td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlOut\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlY\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlN\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n</tr>\n <tr>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlOut1\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlY1\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n    <td>\n        <input id=\"MainContent_chkCtrlN1\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"ctl00$MainContent$chkCtrl\" />\n    </td>\n</tr>\n\nA:\n\nThis can easily be done by writing a couple of lines of jquery. For example see the code below.\n$('input:checkbox').click(function(){\n    $(this).closest('tr').find('input:checkbox').removeProp('checked');\n    $(this).prop('checked',true);\n});\n\njsFiddle: https://jsfiddle.net/taleebanwar/a3qk0kc1/1/\n\nEdit\nAs Tom Stickel has mentioned in the comments using removeProp is a bad idea. It may not work in jquery 2.*. Refer Tom Stickel's answer for a better way to do this.","tokens":["Q",":\n\n","GridView"," Web","Form"," having"," multiple"," checkboxes"," per"," row"," but"," only"," ","1"," per"," row"," is"," allowed"," to"," be"," checked","\n\n","I"," have"," code"," in"," which"," a"," grid","view"," in"," as","p",".net"," web","forms"," sp","its"," out"," ","3"," checkboxes"," of"," which"," I"," would"," like"," to"," have"," J","query"," easily"," traverse"," through"," the"," ID","'s"," and"," ONLY"," allow"," ","1"," checkbox"," per"," row"," to"," be"," checked",".","  \n","They"," will"," Always"," have"," the"," same"," name"," just"," that"," the"," ending"," numbers"," will"," increase"," "," thus"," row"," ","1"," might"," not"," have"," a"," number",","," "," but"," then"," ending"," in"," ","1"," "," then"," ending"," in"," ","2"," ",